+    /// `true` when `subject_ty` is an optional (`T?` Pointer form, or the
+    /// explicit generic `Option<T>` form) whose payload type is a USER enum
+    /// declaring a variant named `None`. For such a subject the interpreter
+    /// reads flat `None` / `nil` / `Some` arms by the payload's own variant
+    /// NAME: a present `Q.None` takes the `None` arm while staying present
+    /// for `.?` / `??` / `if val`. The typed-optional arm probes therefore
+    /// need the stamp-aware `rt_is_none_variant`, not the nil-sentinel-only
+    /// `rt_is_none`. Payloads that are not user enums (or declare no `None`)
+    /// can hold no stamped value, so they keep the cheap probe.
+    /// seed_jit_typed_optional_holding_user_none_takes_some_arm_2026-11-27
